WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:07.040
Quent

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.380
Chirico, you are a PS.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:29.790
Get the proof you seek.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.960
Go, to the planet Quent.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:34.460
Your past lies there.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:36.960
Go, and see for yourself.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.960
A PS...

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.210
A PS...

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.420
A PS!

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:22.330
A PS!

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.000
A PS!

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.380
No!

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.040
A guy'd have to be nuts to try and walk
across the deserts of Quent.

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.210
You're not a Quentian, are you?

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:51.540
I just trade with them. I'm a trader, after all.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:06.330
They only allow us desert traders
to cross the desert with machines.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.250
What's that?

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:10.960
Is that Gomor?

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.830
Yeah, that's it.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.630
The only city on Quent.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.880
I take it you were headed there, too?

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.290
God, what a guy!

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.290
The planet Quent.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.880
Supplier of skilled soldiers
for the past 3,000 years.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:40.210
As long as war continues in the Astragius Galaxy,

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.710
every homeworld will continue to visit this place.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:48.330
Everyone knows there's no better
mercenary than a "Quentman."

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:50.040
Exactly.

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:57.710
Now that we've lost Ypsilon, Chirico has
become an exceptional threat to us.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.250
This will be our final battle with him. Well, then...

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.790
Be careful!

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:05.670
Sir?

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:10.670
Both the Gilgamesh and the Balarant
have troops in Gomor.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.170
Don't worry, sir. We'll be quite discrete.

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:19.330
All that's going to happen will be a slight
disturbance caused by the local ruffians.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.580
They seem confident enough.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:38.250
But that's the privilege of those
who don't know the truth.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:49.330
Would you listen to me, you damned fool?

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.080
Just calm down and sleep!

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.210
Your legs are still shaky!

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:58.670
You could pass out again in your condition!

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:01.420
I feel fine. And I don't have any time to waste.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.710
Time?

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.630
You should be thankful to even be alive!

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:09.920
Besides, I'm not about to let you go
before getting a reward for saving you!

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.380
You'll get plenty of reward, later!

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:21.130
Don't get me wrong.
This place is crawling with drifters.

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:23.460
A guy who doesn't know the ropes can get hurt!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.290
Let go of me.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.580
What do you want to do, anyway?

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.750
I want to meet a Quentian.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:32.420
A Quentman?

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:34.130
In this city?

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:37.380
Hey, wait a minute!

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:46.750
Look, do you see a single Quentman here?

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:52.630
Gomor may be the only city on Quent,

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.710
but everyone living here is an off-worlder.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:56.670
What about their government?

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:59.790
Not here. Nothing of theirs is in this city.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:03.330
The only time they ever come
is when mercenaries are recruited.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.210
And now?

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.540
They just shipped some out three days ago.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:10.540
There'd only be one or two Quentmen
at the Merc Center now.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.380
I see.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.420
Hey, if you want to meet one that badly,
I'll take you with me on my next trade run.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:18.880
Hey!

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.380
Suit yourself.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.580
Mr. Hazegar!

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.040
When did you get back, Gecko?

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:51.290
You mind putting me down? I can't breathe!

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:52.290
Drop him.

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:59.880
You picked up a strange guy
in the desert, didn't you?

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:03.630
The only thing on the route
he was taking was your caravan.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:07.330
His name's Chirico, right? Let me have him!

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:10.130
Well, that is...

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:18.380
Okay, okay! I'll tell you!

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:21.210
Yeah, I picked the guy up.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.000
Nice to hear the truth from you.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.080
Okay, where is he?

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.960
Sir, I'm a trader.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:34.000
I'd like some compensation
for this valuable information.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:34.920
You piece of-!

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:35.880
It's all right.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.460
I'll give you a reward.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:46.710
This much?

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:47.670
Where is he?

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:49.830
He's headed for the Mercenary Center.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:53.750
Oh, but he said he was gonna do
a little shopping first.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:54.880
Move it!

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:02.750
Well, I'll be damned.
500 balants from that tightwad?

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.710
This must be something big.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.330
Is this the reception desk?

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:30.710
Yes, sir.

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:32.750
I want a Quentman.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.790
What's your government affiliation?

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:38.040
More importantly, what's your billing number?

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:39.790
I don't have one.

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:42.130
I want a mercenary for a private mission.

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:44.500
Impossible.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:47.210
The money's already been paid.
Check it out for yourself.

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.290
Uh, one moment, please.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.380
Wha...? Where are you going, sir?

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:21.710
To all guards! Be on the lookout for an intruder
in the vicinity of the level 2 office block!

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:23.500
There are Quentmen here, right? Where are they?

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:25.040
What are you doing?

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.040
Answer me!

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.580
Level 8, room 600!

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.750
Don't play games with me!
That's the statistics office!

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:37.670
Level 7. Half the west wing's
for the Quentmen to live in.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:38.710
There he is!

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:39.920
This way!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:59.290
To all guards! Be on the lookout for an intruder
in the vicinity of the level 2 office block!

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:04.250
Repeat! Be on the lookout for an intruder
in the vicinity of the level 2 office block!

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:47.750
Are you a Quentian?

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.500
I won't do anything. I just want to talk.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.790
It won't lock. You broke it.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:03.040
Sorry. Any more of you here?

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:05.960
Just me.

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:17.540
Tell me, does the term "PS" mean anything to you?

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.210
Perfect Soldier?

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:21.880
No.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.380
Do you know if any other Quentians
might know about it?

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:28.580
Perhaps, but I'm not sure.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.250
I have to find out.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:33.330
Where can I find a lot of Quentians?

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.670
Don't you people have some sort of government?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.960
Long ago, we did.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.500
But now we've broken up into tribes.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.330
Many, many tribes.

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:47.330
Since they're scattered all across Quent, we don't
even know how many of us there actually are.

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:49.580
But, then how do you recruit mercenaries?

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:52.580
How do you gather tens of thousands
for the Gilgamesh and Balarant?

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:57.630
I am the Emissary.
I tell my people how many are needed.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:02.630
Those who wish to become soldiers
gather of their own volition.

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:07.000
Then tell your people about me.
Where's your communicator?

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.250
How do you contact them?

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:14.540
Emissary! Please open the door!
We think the intruder's in there!

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.040
I can't keep the door closed.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:24.210
Besides, those who want a door open
will force it open eventually.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:27.420
Tell me! How do you contact them?

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:29.920
The beacon.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:32.210
"Beacon?"

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:37.960
I can't do it here and there's no time to teach you.

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.830
Emissary, please answer!

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:42.830
If you don't answer in one minute,
we'll blow the door open!

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:49.580
If it's that important to you, you will meet
as many Quentians as is possible.

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:53.540
None of my people will resist you.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:57.420
We may be known as mercenaries,
but we love peace most of all.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.420
Cross the desert.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:08.130
I will.

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:18.000
Sorry about this.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.920
Down! Get below him!

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:13.080
He's headed for Gecko's place.
Cut him off at Third Street!

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:16.670
But, Boss! He actually got out of
the Merc Center in one piece!

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:18.670
He must have balls of steel!

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:21.790
He's supposed to be unbeatable in an AT.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.250
But this'll be enough for when he's naked.

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:43.880
You finally came, Chirico.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:44.750
Who are you?

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.920
We won't give you back to
the guards at the Center.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:49.790
Who are you working for?

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:54.130
Old friends of yours.
They're waiting for us at the space port.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:00.960
After him! Cut him off!

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:08.710
Chirico!

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:11.290
Gecko!

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:14.420
Sorry. I told them about you.

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:16.420
Throw me something! Hurry!

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:20.000
You'll be okay. Just let 'em catch you for now.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.210
Why don't you relax?

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:27.130
They've captured Chirico
and are on their way here.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.170
That was easy.

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:34.920
Well, think about it.
We usually go after him with ATs.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.460
Ah, sarcasm!

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:43.710
Here they come.

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.670
All right, hand him over!

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:01.960
First the money!
I want double what you promised me!

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.540
You what?

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:07.670
Look at me! That guy isn't human!

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:10.500
A tranq that could drop a tiger
or a snake couldn't stop him!

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.710
All right. Bring him up!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.250
Mr. Mayor!

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:42.670
Hazegar, I'll explain later,
but you have to hand that man over to me.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:45.130
This is my business!

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:47.170
You can't stop me just because you're the mayor!

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:51.080
That man is apparently
a special guest of a Quentman!

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:52.580
A Quentman?

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.210
He's in the car.

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:00.710
This is Quent. We have to do what they say.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:02.380
You know that, don't you?

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:25.000
Ru... Ru Shako?

00:20:25.710 --> 00:20:27.380
We meet again.

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:29.250
How did you find me?

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:31.580
The beacon.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.580
A man named Gecko told us.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:40.170
Just one word was sent: "Chirico."

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:44.670
I really owe him. Thanks, both of you.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:47.540
You're building up quite a debt, aren't you?

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:05.500
We didn't realize he'd contacted a Quentian.

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:10.080
He'll now most likely be headed
for one of their villages.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.830
Once they leave the city, they'll be easy targets.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.920
I see. Make preparations for the operation.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.130
Yes, sir!

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:30.130
Chirico came to Quent
specifically to meet a Quentman.

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:33.920
Why?

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:43.290
Presents. Take 'em.

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:50.080
Okay, let's get going.

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:52.380
Where?

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:54.500
To my village, first of all.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:57.000
And there, will anyone know?

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:00.130
Can they tell me about PSs? About who I am?

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:03.630
Who can say?

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:38.040
Our reunion on Quent
could be called miraculous.

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:41.880
With uncertainty and anticipation
mixing within me,

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:44.290
I stepped forward into an unknown world.

00:22:46.250 --> 00:22:49.250
What awaited me at the end of this desert?

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.330 --> 00:23:00.460
Did they abandon civilization?
Or did civilization abandon them?

00:23:00.830 --> 00:23:03.670
Wandering through the flow of eternity,

00:23:03.670 --> 00:23:07.460
the mysterious Quentians came to live
at the bottom of valleys.

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:09.830
What was it they sought?

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:12.420
What was it they so feared?

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:16.380
The secrets of the Astragius Galaxy
lie sleeping on this world.

00:23:17.210 --> 00:23:19.330
Next time, "The Desert"

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:24.290
The Desert

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:22.670
Lightning strikes from across 3,000 years.

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Brighter than any other light...
